# main-overview

## Development Guidelines

- Only modify code directly relevant to the specific request. Avoid changing unrelated functionality.
- Never replace code with placeholders like `# ... rest of the processing ...`. Always include complete code.
- Break problems into smaller steps. Think through each step separately before implementing.
- Always provide a complete PLAN with REASONING based on evidence from code and logs before making changes.
- Explain your OBSERVATIONS clearly, then provide REASONING to identify the exact issue. Add console logs when needed to gather more information.


The documentation system is organized around core CouchCMS domain concepts, structured in a hierarchical manner:

## Documentation Structure
- Domain-specific sections divide content into logical areas:
  - Getting Started
  - Concepts 
  - Tags Reference
  - Add-Ons
  - Tutorials

## New Feature Documentation
Specially marked sections highlight recent platform additions:
- Sub-Templates functionality
- Template Inheritance system
- Custom Routes implementation
- Extended Entities framework

## Media Integration
A specialized media presentation system handles documentation content:
- Unified media card system for consistent content display
- Integrated video documentation support through YouTube embedding
- Maintained aspect ratio standards for visual documentation elements

Importance Score: 45
Primary value comes from the domain-specific organization of CouchCMS documentation components, though implementation remains fairly standard.

